{
  "__inputs": [
    {
      "name": "DS_PROMETHEUS",
      "label": "Prometheus",
      "description": "Prometheus datasource holding CNPG and kube-state-metrics series",
      "type": "datasource",
      "pluginId": "prometheus",
      "pluginName": "Prometheus"
    }
  ],
  "annotations": {
    "list": []
  },
  "description": "Reference dashboard for CloudNativePG health on one Kubernetes cluster, scoped by namespace. Requires a k8s_cluster_name label on the queried series. Not deployed by nke-stack. Empty panels are expected when CNPG is not installed.",
  "editable": true,
  "fiscalYearStartMonth": 0,
  "graphTooltip": 1,
  "id": null,
  "links": [],
  "panels": [
    {
      "id": 0,
      "type": "text",
      "title": "Requirements and scope",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 12,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "### Scope\nReference dashboard for CloudNativePG (CNPG) health on one Kubernetes cluster, scoped by namespace. It is not deployed by the nke-stack composition. Import this JSON and select a Prometheus datasource.\n\n### When this applies\nThe default nke-stack install uses a single PostgreSQL instance, not CNPG. This dashboard is for sites that run CNPG (the site-controller overlay typically uses namespaces `cnpg-cloud`, `cnpg-site`, and `cnpg-temporal`). Empty panels mean CNPG is not installed or not scraped; they are not a failure.\n\n### Assumptions\n- Series carry a `k8s_cluster_name` label identifying the Kubernetes cluster (Prometheus label from the OpenTelemetry resource attribute `k8s.cluster.name`). CNPG's own `cluster` label is the **Postgres** Cluster resource name; it is kept in joins and legends, not as a dashboard variable. Scope by `$namespace` instead (typically one Cluster CR per namespace).\n- `$namespace` selects one or more CNPG namespaces.\n\n### Metric dependencies\n- **CNPG collector:** `cnpg_collector_fencing_on`, `cnpg_pg_replication_lag`, `cnpg_pg_replication_streaming_replicas`, `cnpg_pg_replication_in_recovery`, `cnpg_pg_replication_slots_*`, `cnpg_pg_stat_archiver_*`, `cnpg_backends_total`, `cnpg_pg_settings_setting`\n- **kube-state-metrics (optional):** `kube_customresource_cnpg_cluster_status_phase` if the CNPG Cluster CRD is exported; otherwise Cluster phase stays empty\n- **kubelet volume stats:** `kubelet_volume_stats_used_bytes` / `kubelet_volume_stats_capacity_bytes` for PVC fill\n- **kube-state-metrics:** `kube_pod_container_status_restarts_total` for container restarts\n\nNo replica count is assumed. A single CNPG instance is a valid topology."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 1,
      "type": "row",
      "title": "Cluster Status",
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 12
      },
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Cluster phase",
      "description": "CNPG Cluster.status.phase from kube-state-metrics CRD metrics. Cluster in healthy state is the expected value. Empty when the CRD is not exported.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 13
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
          },
          "expr": "kube_customresource_cnpg_cluster_status_phase{k8s_cluster_name=~\"$cluster\",namespace=~\"$namespace\"} == 1",
          "legendFormat": "{{namespace}}/{{name}}: {{phase}}",
          "refId": "A",
          "instant": true,
          "range": false
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "color": {
            "fixedColor": "text",
            "mode": "fixed"
          },
          "decimals": 0
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "none",
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "textMode": "auto"
      }
    },
